Assignment 2 – Setup Proof (VS Code, Node.js, Live Server)

Objective

To understand the basic setup required for web development using Visual Studio Code, Node.js, and the Live Server extension.

Tools Required

1. Visual Studio Code (VS Code)

Visual Studio Code is a code editor used to write and edit HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files.

2. Node.js

Node.js allows JavaScript to run outside the browser. Its installation can be verified using the following commands in the terminal:

node -v
npm -v

3. Live Server

Live Server is a VS Code extension that launches a local development server and displays HTML pages in a browser.

Setup Verification

Tool| Verification
VS Code| Editor setup to be verified
Node.js| Check using "node -v"
npm| Check using "npm -v"
Live Server| Install and test in VS Code

